WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.133 --> 00:00:01.201
Major breaking news over

00:00:01.201 --> 00:00:02.402
the United States Supreme Court

00:00:02.402 --> 00:00:02.836
right now.

00:00:02.836 --> 00:00:03.970
CNN's Jessica Schneider

00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:05.071
is on the scene for us.

00:00:05.071 --> 00:00:06.272
What are you learning, Jessica?

00:00:06.272 --> 00:00:07.440
Well, Wolf, the Supreme Court

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.209
has just handed down

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:10.110
their decision

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:11.478
on the application for that

00:00:11.478 --> 00:00:12.412
stay requested

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:13.713
by the Biden administration.

00:00:13.713 --> 00:00:15.181
And it is, in fact,

00:00:15.181 --> 00:00:17.317
a win for the Biden administration.

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.652
The FDA, the Supreme Court here saying

00:00:19.953 --> 00:00:21.788
that all of those restrictions

00:00:21.788 --> 00:00:22.989
that the Fifth Circuit had wanted

00:00:22.989 --> 00:00:24.657
to put on the abortion pill.

00:00:24.657 --> 00:00:25.592
They're saying that

00:00:25.592 --> 00:00:26.526
all of those restrictions

00:00:26.526 --> 00:00:28.094
will not take effect.

00:00:28.094 --> 00:00:30.330
So it will continue to be status quo

00:00:30.597 --> 00:00:31.631
for mifepristone

00:00:31.631 --> 00:00:33.133
in the way it's administered

00:00:33.133 --> 00:00:34.434
while the appeals process

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.836
plays out in the Fifth Circuit.

00:00:36.836 --> 00:00:38.104
This is something we've you know,

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.239
this is the third time

00:00:39.239 --> 00:00:40.874
the Supreme Court has issued

00:00:40.874 --> 00:00:42.709
something related to this case.

00:00:42.709 --> 00:00:43.843
It took a little longer.

00:00:43.843 --> 00:00:44.911
We were expecting something

00:00:44.911 --> 00:00:46.046
perhaps on Wednesday.

00:00:46.046 --> 00:00:47.380
And here we are Friday night.

00:00:47.380 --> 00:00:47.580
And we're

00:00:47.580 --> 00:00:48.681
now seeing

00:00:48.681 --> 00:00:49.416
that the reason

00:00:49.416 --> 00:00:51.451
it took a little bit longer than expected

00:00:51.451 --> 00:00:53.653
is because there was a dissent

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:54.721
from this from Justice

00:00:54.721 --> 00:00:55.588
Clarence Thomas

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.290
and then also a dissent from Justice

00:00:57.290 --> 00:00:58.591
Samuel Alito.

00:00:58.591 --> 00:00:59.025
Justice

00:00:59.025 --> 00:00:59.726
Alito did

00:00:59.726 --> 00:01:01.861
write about four pages of dissent

00:01:02.262 --> 00:01:02.929
saying why

00:01:02.929 --> 00:01:04.497
he would have let those restrictions

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.365
go into effect,

00:01:05.365 --> 00:01:07.967
why a stay he believed wasn't warranted.

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.370
But the takeaway here is that,

00:01:10.370 --> 00:01:12.605
you know, this will help the FDA.

00:01:12.605 --> 00:01:15.341
The FDA had warned of chaos and confusion

00:01:15.575 --> 00:01:17.777
if the stay had not been continued,

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.079
if the stay had not been granted

00:01:19.079 --> 00:01:20.380
by the Supreme Court.

00:01:20.380 --> 00:01:22.849
So now things will remain, as it's been

00:01:22.849 --> 00:01:25.218
for the past weeks and months and years

00:01:25.552 --> 00:01:26.786
as this case continues

00:01:26.786 --> 00:01:28.455
to play out in the lower courts,

00:01:28.455 --> 00:01:29.789
because the lower court here,

00:01:29.789 --> 00:01:31.791
the Fifth Circuit, has really fast

00:01:31.791 --> 00:01:33.159
tracked this appeal.

00:01:33.159 --> 00:01:34.594
They have set a very fast

00:01:34.594 --> 00:01:35.762
briefing schedule.

00:01:35.762 --> 00:01:36.563
Oral arguments

00:01:36.563 --> 00:01:38.865
will be in less than a month on May, 17th

00:01:38.865 --> 00:01:41.101
so the underlying issue in this case

00:01:41.101 --> 00:01:41.434
as to

00:01:41.434 --> 00:01:43.203
whether the FDA went through the proper

00:01:43.203 --> 00:01:45.705
procedures to grant approval

00:01:45.705 --> 00:01:47.040
for mifepristone.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:48.875
That case will play out

00:01:48.875 --> 00:01:50.877
while everything else is on hold.

00:01:50.877 --> 00:01:51.911
So it will be status

00:01:51.911 --> 00:01:53.813
quo for this drug until the

00:01:53.813 --> 00:01:54.481
the Fifth Circuit,

00:01:54.481 --> 00:01:55.148
I'm sorry,

00:01:55.148 --> 00:01:56.749
can actually hear these arguments

00:01:56.749 --> 00:01:57.684
and then make a decision.

00:01:57.684 --> 00:01:58.618
But, Wolf,

00:01:58.618 --> 00:01:59.652
it is very likely

00:01:59.652 --> 00:02:01.087
that this is not the last time

00:02:01.087 --> 00:02:01.788
the Supreme Court

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:02.789
will weigh in on this

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.691
after the arguments play out

00:02:04.691 --> 00:02:06.359
and are decided in the Fifth Circuit.

00:02:06.359 --> 00:02:07.727
It is very likely

00:02:07.727 --> 00:02:08.228
that either

00:02:08.228 --> 00:02:08.862
party, the party

00:02:08.862 --> 00:02:10.263
that loses, will appeal

00:02:10.263 --> 00:02:11.231
this to the Supreme Court.

00:02:11.231 --> 00:02:12.432
But for now,

00:02:12.432 --> 00:02:14.100
a win for the Biden administration

00:02:14.100 --> 00:02:14.767
and all things

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:16.503
stay status quo, meaning

00:02:16.503 --> 00:02:17.403
women can continue

00:02:17.403 --> 00:02:19.772
to access this abortion pill as they have

00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:22.108
previously Wolf.

00:02:22.108 --> 00:02:23.743
Very significant news indeed.

00:02:23.743 --> 00:02:25.078
I want to bring in Joan Biskupic,

00:02:25.078 --> 00:02:25.812
who studies

00:02:25.812 --> 00:02:26.613
the Supreme Court

00:02:26.613 --> 00:02:28.181
for us, knows a lot about it.

00:02:28.181 --> 00:02:29.649
Give us your reaction, Joe.

00:02:29.649 --> 00:02:31.451
I think this is a really important

00:02:31.451 --> 00:02:33.119
signal from the Supreme Court

00:02:33.119 --> 00:02:33.753
that we are

00:02:33.753 --> 00:02:35.688
in a different kind of lawsuit now.

00:02:35.688 --> 00:02:37.257
This is much different than what happened

00:02:37.257 --> 00:02:37.991
last June

00:02:37.991 --> 00:02:39.826
when the justices rolled back

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:41.461
constitutional abortion rights,

00:02:41.461 --> 00:02:43.062
but said that abortion

00:02:43.062 --> 00:02:44.831
could still be legal in the states

00:02:44.831 --> 00:02:46.166
that so chose.

00:02:46.166 --> 00:02:47.367
And if they had gone

00:02:47.367 --> 00:02:49.102
in any other direction here,

00:02:49.102 --> 00:02:51.404
it would have been backtracking

00:02:51.404 --> 00:02:52.939
on their promise of states

00:02:52.939 --> 00:02:54.774
being able to do what they wanted.

00:02:54.774 --> 00:02:55.975
And one thing I would

00:02:55.975 --> 00:02:57.977
stress here is the lower court

00:02:57.977 --> 00:02:59.646
judges who acted in this case

00:02:59.646 --> 00:03:02.782
were really out on the outer limits here.

00:03:03.116 --> 00:03:03.583
They were going

00:03:03.583 --> 00:03:05.218
beyond what the Supreme Court

00:03:05.218 --> 00:03:07.053
had had said back in June.

00:03:07.053 --> 00:03:08.922
Judge, because Merrick, the

00:03:08.922 --> 00:03:09.722
who heard the case

00:03:09.722 --> 00:03:11.925
originally in Amarillo, Texas,

00:03:12.225 --> 00:03:14.460
had really imposed his own moral

00:03:14.460 --> 00:03:15.929
and policy decisions here.

00:03:15.929 --> 00:03:16.129
I mean,

00:03:16.129 --> 00:03:17.730
he acknowledged that he was second

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.032
guessing the FDA.

00:03:19.032 --> 00:03:19.866
And he acknowledged

00:03:19.866 --> 00:03:22.335
he used language that certainly showed

00:03:22.502 --> 00:03:24.003
where he stood relative

00:03:24.003 --> 00:03:25.772
to abortion rights

00:03:25.772 --> 00:03:27.540
straightly against them.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:29.709
And then the original appellate court

00:03:29.709 --> 00:03:30.877
that had

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.580
affirmed a portion of that decision

00:03:33.780 --> 00:03:34.747
had also shown

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:36.316
that it was willing to engage

00:03:36.316 --> 00:03:38.084
in essentially a policy analysis

00:03:38.084 --> 00:03:38.952
by putting itself

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.186
into the shoes

00:03:40.186 --> 00:03:41.321
of the FDA

00:03:41.321 --> 00:03:43.356
and its own scientific determinations.

00:03:43.356 --> 00:03:45.391
And the Supreme Court has pulled back.

00:03:45.391 --> 00:03:46.893
You know, again, as Jessica said,

00:03:46.893 --> 00:03:48.895
we don't know what will eventually happen

00:03:48.895 --> 00:03:51.264
when it resolves the merits of this case.

00:03:51.397 --> 00:03:52.832
But I think what we're seeing now

00:03:52.832 --> 00:03:53.766
from the Supreme Court

00:03:53.766 --> 00:03:54.033
at this

00:03:54.033 --> 00:03:55.101
point is

00:03:55.101 --> 00:03:57.403
they are not going to try to extend

00:03:57.570 --> 00:04:00.540
kind of this aggressive anti-abortion

00:04:01.140 --> 00:04:03.543
movement against what states individually

00:04:03.543 --> 00:04:04.477
want to do

00:04:04.477 --> 00:04:06.813
and against a federal agency

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.648
that approved this drug

00:04:08.648 --> 00:04:09.782
dating back to the year

00:04:09.782 --> 00:04:12.719
2000 has done its own

00:04:13.019 --> 00:04:14.520
scientific determinations

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:16.623
about its safety and effectiveness.

00:04:16.623 --> 00:04:18.191
It's not in a position to second

00:04:18.191 --> 00:04:20.860
guess that at this crucial

00:04:21.361 --> 00:04:23.596
but still temporary pointed the case.

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.865
Steve Vladeck, I'm anxious to get your

00:04:25.865 --> 00:04:27.133
reaction as well. Go ahead.

00:04:28.868 --> 00:04:29.068
Yeah.

00:04:29.068 --> 00:04:29.402
Hey, Wolf.

00:04:29.402 --> 00:04:31.170
I think John has it exactly right.

00:04:31.170 --> 00:04:31.671
And I would just

00:04:31.671 --> 00:04:32.605
add, you know,

00:04:32.605 --> 00:04:34.107
I think this actually isn't

00:04:34.107 --> 00:04:35.541
that big of a surprise

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.210
because of the chaos

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.678
we would have seen

00:04:38.678 --> 00:04:40.013
at midnight tonight

00:04:40.013 --> 00:04:40.813
if Judge

00:04:40.813 --> 00:04:42.882
Merrick long had gone into effect.

00:04:42.882 --> 00:04:44.050
It's not the court

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:46.219
telling us how they might rule eventually

00:04:46.486 --> 00:04:48.554
if the question of mifepristone access

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:50.823
reaches them in a normal appeal.

00:04:51.024 --> 00:04:52.592
It's not the court saying,

00:04:52.592 --> 00:04:53.860
you know, we disagree

00:04:53.860 --> 00:04:56.162
necessarily with the reasoning below,

00:04:56.162 --> 00:04:57.597
but it is the court saying

00:04:57.597 --> 00:04:59.198
that when we balance the equities,

00:04:59.198 --> 00:05:01.668
when we look at the potential harm

00:05:01.934 --> 00:05:03.936
of letting this decision go into effect,

00:05:04.170 --> 00:05:05.505
while the appeal works its way

00:05:05.505 --> 00:05:06.406
through the courts

00:05:06.406 --> 00:05:08.174
versus keeping it on hold,

00:05:08.174 --> 00:05:09.909
that that seems to be very

00:05:09.909 --> 00:05:11.110
one sided here.

00:05:11.110 --> 00:05:11.611
Critically,

00:05:11.611 --> 00:05:12.779
I think this is an important point.

00:05:12.779 --> 00:05:13.546
The case now

00:05:13.546 --> 00:05:14.781
will proceed

00:05:14.781 --> 00:05:15.782
in the Fifth Circuit,

00:05:15.782 --> 00:05:17.450
in the federal appeals court

00:05:17.450 --> 00:05:18.451
in New Orleans.

00:05:18.451 --> 00:05:19.352
And one of the things

00:05:19.352 --> 00:05:20.787
we ought to keep an eye on

00:05:20.787 --> 00:05:22.422
is whether that court now

00:05:22.422 --> 00:05:24.257
looks at tonight's ruling

00:05:24.257 --> 00:05:25.892
and says the writing's on the wall,

00:05:25.892 --> 00:05:26.826
whether that court actually

00:05:26.826 --> 00:05:28.728
is now more skeptical of Judge Kavanaugh.

00:05:28.728 --> 00:05:29.629
It's related,

00:05:29.629 --> 00:05:30.630
such that

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:31.097
this case

00:05:31.097 --> 00:05:32.298
might never even come back

00:05:32.298 --> 00:05:33.733
to the Supreme Court

00:05:33.733 --> 00:05:35.301
Either way, the headline

00:05:35.301 --> 00:05:35.935
for right now

00:05:35.935 --> 00:05:37.203
is that mifepristone

00:05:37.203 --> 00:05:39.572
access tomorrow is going to be the same

00:05:39.572 --> 00:05:40.740
as it was yesterday,

00:05:40.740 --> 00:05:41.874
but that's not going to change

00:05:41.874 --> 00:05:43.376
any time soon.

00:05:43.376 --> 00:05:44.577
And that the appellate process

00:05:44.577 --> 00:05:46.412
is not going to run its normal

00:05:46.412 --> 00:05:49.382
as opposed to chaotic emergency course.

00:05:50.516 --> 00:05:51.250
Elizabeth Cohen is

00:05:51.250 --> 00:05:52.685
our senior medical correspondent.

00:05:52.685 --> 00:05:54.120
So what does this mean, Elizabeth,

00:05:54.120 --> 00:05:56.356
for women and health care providers,

00:05:56.556 --> 00:05:57.590
for that matter, here

00:05:57.590 --> 00:05:59.325
in the United States?

00:06:00.893 --> 00:06:03.096
So, Wolf, I think we can hear

00:06:03.096 --> 00:06:04.931
OB-GYNs across the country

00:06:04.931 --> 00:06:07.300
breathing a sigh of relief

00:06:07.300 --> 00:06:08.368
that this has happened

00:06:08.368 --> 00:06:10.002
this way, that for at least a certain

00:06:10.002 --> 00:06:11.170
period of time,

00:06:11.170 --> 00:06:13.206
they will be able to use mifepristone.

00:06:13.206 --> 00:06:14.640
This is a drug that they use

00:06:14.640 --> 00:06:16.142
to take care of women

00:06:16.142 --> 00:06:17.577
who are having miscarriages,

00:06:17.577 --> 00:06:19.011
who are having abortions.

00:06:19.011 --> 00:06:19.879
And it is

00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:22.048
it has been shown for 20 years,

00:06:22.181 --> 00:06:23.750
20 years to be safe.

00:06:23.750 --> 00:06:24.117
In fact,

00:06:24.117 --> 00:06:25.251
fewer deadly

00:06:25.251 --> 00:06:25.852
side effects

00:06:25.852 --> 00:06:28.254
than penicillin, fewer than Viagra.

00:06:28.354 --> 00:06:29.956
And now they can keep using it.

00:06:29.956 --> 00:06:31.891
If this decision had gone the other way

00:06:31.891 --> 00:06:32.925
and they weren't allowed

00:06:32.925 --> 00:06:34.527
to give mifepristone,

00:06:34.527 --> 00:06:36.429
they would have given the other drugs

00:06:36.429 --> 00:06:37.497
that this is used with.

00:06:37.497 --> 00:06:38.898
It's called might a possible.

00:06:38.898 --> 00:06:40.433
They would have had to have used that

00:06:40.433 --> 00:06:41.801
on its own.

00:06:41.801 --> 00:06:43.703
And that is an inferior treatment.

00:06:43.703 --> 00:06:44.871
So talking to doctors

00:06:44.871 --> 00:06:45.571
for the past few weeks,

00:06:45.571 --> 00:06:46.139
they said,

00:06:46.139 --> 00:06:47.173
why in the world

00:06:47.173 --> 00:06:48.841
when I want to give my patients

00:06:48.841 --> 00:06:50.576
and inferior treatment

00:06:50.576 --> 00:06:51.310
that I know

00:06:51.310 --> 00:06:53.146
is going to put them at a higher risk

00:06:53.146 --> 00:06:53.613
for having

00:06:53.613 --> 00:06:54.180
what could be

00:06:54.180 --> 00:06:56.282
potentially serious complications?

00:06:56.282 --> 00:06:57.950
I should be giving my patients

00:06:57.950 --> 00:06:59.252
the best treatment treatment

00:06:59.252 --> 00:07:01.320
that's been studied in clinical trials

00:07:01.320 --> 00:07:03.022
and approved by the FDA.

00:07:03.022 --> 00:07:04.290
So I think there will be

00:07:04.290 --> 00:07:06.325
a feeling of great relief,

00:07:06.325 --> 00:07:07.093
but also a bit

00:07:07.093 --> 00:07:08.361
of a feeling of trepidation.

00:07:08.361 --> 00:07:08.694
All right.

00:07:08.694 --> 00:07:10.530
What happens after this certain

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:11.564
period of time?

00:07:11.564 --> 00:07:13.766
What might change in the future?

00:07:13.933 --> 00:07:14.333
Well,

00:07:14.333 --> 00:07:15.134
we'll see what happens

00:07:15.134 --> 00:07:16.335
down the road, Dana.

00:07:16.335 --> 00:07:17.503
Dana Bash is still with us.

00:07:17.503 --> 00:07:18.070
Dana, talk

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:18.471
a little bit

00:07:18.471 --> 00:07:20.373
about the politics of all of this

00:07:20.373 --> 00:07:21.707
and how big of a win

00:07:21.707 --> 00:07:22.842
this is for the White House

00:07:22.842 --> 00:07:25.244
and for Democrats, for that matter.

00:07:25.244 --> 00:07:26.612
Well, it absolutely is a big win.

00:07:26.612 --> 00:07:28.214
That's exactly how Jessica Schneider,

00:07:28.214 --> 00:07:30.316
when she broke the news, described it.

00:07:30.616 --> 00:07:31.651
But Elizabeth talked

00:07:31.651 --> 00:07:34.821
about the sigh of relief in India

00:07:34.821 --> 00:07:38.891
among obstetricians across the country.

00:07:38.891 --> 00:07:40.960
I think that there is definitely

00:07:40.960 --> 00:07:42.361
a sigh of relief

00:07:42.361 --> 00:07:43.296
that is much less

00:07:43.296 --> 00:07:45.698
audible, much more private

00:07:45.698 --> 00:07:47.333
among Republicans

00:07:47.333 --> 00:07:49.168
and all you need to do is

00:07:49.168 --> 00:07:50.903
look at how Republicans

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:52.672
who are either on Capitol Hill

00:07:52.672 --> 00:07:53.739
or more specifically,

00:07:53.739 --> 00:07:56.976
those who are vying to be the Republican

00:07:57.310 --> 00:07:58.911
presidential nominee

00:07:58.911 --> 00:08:00.646
have had a lot of trouble

00:08:00.646 --> 00:08:02.582
figuring out where to stand

00:08:02.582 --> 00:08:04.050
on this issue,

00:08:04.050 --> 00:08:07.053
because it's the question of being

00:08:07.487 --> 00:08:08.821
sort of anti-abortion

00:08:08.821 --> 00:08:09.589
is one thing,

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:11.791
but also being for states

00:08:11.791 --> 00:08:13.392
rights is another.

00:08:13.392 --> 00:08:14.760
And what the Supreme Court did,

00:08:14.760 --> 00:08:16.329
at least for the time being,

00:08:16.329 --> 00:08:19.065
is allowed them to continue with it

00:08:19.065 --> 00:08:20.633
if they so choose

00:08:20.633 --> 00:08:22.168
that consistent argument

00:08:22.168 --> 00:08:24.437
that it is up to the states

00:08:24.704 --> 00:08:26.439
to deal with abortion

00:08:26.439 --> 00:08:28.908
and it should not be a federal decision

00:08:29.108 --> 00:08:30.643
to just completely do away

00:08:30.643 --> 00:08:33.880
with this medication, which is Elizabeth

00:08:33.880 --> 00:08:34.413
just said

00:08:34.413 --> 00:08:36.616
has been proven time and time again

00:08:36.616 --> 00:08:37.783
for two decades.

00:08:37.783 --> 00:08:39.118
To be quite safe

00:08:39.118 --> 00:08:40.653
not just for abortion,

00:08:40.653 --> 00:08:43.022
but for other medical issues

00:08:43.022 --> 00:08:44.590
like dealing with women

00:08:44.590 --> 00:08:45.858
who have miscarriages.

00:08:45.858 --> 00:08:46.826
And Steve Vladeck,

00:08:46.826 --> 00:08:48.294
I saw you nodding, so go ahead.

00:08:48.294 --> 00:08:48.995
Give us your thought.

00:08:50.796 --> 00:08:52.231
No, I mean, I think that's right.

00:08:52.231 --> 00:08:52.832
I mean, I think both.

00:08:52.832 --> 00:08:53.566
But the other side

00:08:53.566 --> 00:08:55.535
and what Elizabeth said is exactly right.

00:08:55.535 --> 00:08:56.402
And, you know,

00:08:56.402 --> 00:08:58.471
I think what this really does

00:08:58.471 --> 00:09:00.706
is this reminds us of the difference

00:09:00.940 --> 00:09:02.742
between how this kind of litigation

00:09:02.742 --> 00:09:04.176
is supposed to go

00:09:04.176 --> 00:09:06.345
and how it's increasingly going

00:09:06.345 --> 00:09:07.413
the way that the legal system

00:09:07.413 --> 00:09:07.980
has been acting

00:09:07.980 --> 00:09:09.282
in the last couple of years.

00:09:09.282 --> 00:09:10.583
It's not normal, Wolf,

00:09:10.583 --> 00:09:10.917
for us

00:09:10.917 --> 00:09:12.585
to be having these kinds of late

00:09:12.585 --> 00:09:13.719
Friday night

00:09:13.719 --> 00:09:16.022
fire drills where we're worrying about

00:09:16.522 --> 00:09:19.559
in 5 hours is nationwide access

00:09:19.559 --> 00:09:21.294
to this vital medication

00:09:21.294 --> 00:09:23.296
going to be entirely disrupted.

00:09:23.563 --> 00:09:25.398
And so I think it's another possible way

00:09:25.398 --> 00:09:27.366
of looking at tonight's rule in that

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:28.534
the Supreme Court, rather

00:09:28.534 --> 00:09:29.335
than necessarily

00:09:29.335 --> 00:09:30.269
signaling a view

00:09:30.269 --> 00:09:32.572
on the crystal question specifically,

00:09:32.905 --> 00:09:33.839
is absolutely signal

00:09:33.839 --> 00:09:34.740
a view on sort of

00:09:34.740 --> 00:09:35.975
letting this work its way

00:09:35.975 --> 00:09:36.976
through the courts.

00:09:36.976 --> 00:09:39.145
Without disrupting the entire

00:09:39.245 --> 00:09:41.280
health system in the process.

00:09:41.514 --> 00:09:41.614
You know,

00:09:41.614 --> 00:09:43.583
I think that's a return to normal

00:09:43.583 --> 00:09:45.585
predictability, as Elizabeth says,

00:09:45.585 --> 00:09:46.986
for medical providers

00:09:46.986 --> 00:09:47.486
it creates

00:09:47.486 --> 00:09:49.488
maybe some more political predictability.

00:09:49.722 --> 00:09:51.891
And frankly, Wolf, from my perspective,

00:09:51.891 --> 00:09:54.360
it's really a much more realistic

00:09:54.360 --> 00:09:57.263
and I think even keeled way.

00:09:57.263 --> 00:09:57.530
Right.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:09:58.331
For the legal system

00:09:58.331 --> 00:10:00.166
to be handling these kinds of disputes.

